Let $C$ be a smooth irreducible projective curve of genus $g \ge 2$ over $\mathbb{C}$. A coherent system of type $(n,d,k)$ on $C$ is a pair $(E,V)$ where $E$ is a vector bundle on $C$ of rank $n$ and degree $d$, and $V \subseteq H^0(E)$ is a linear subspace of dimension $k$. For a real parameter $\alpha$, the $\alpha$-slope of $(E,V)$ is $\mu_\alpha(E,V) = d/n + \alpha k/n$, and $(E,V)$ is $\alpha$-(semi)stable if for every proper coherent subsystem $(E',V')$ with $0 < \mathrm{rk}(E') < n$ one has $\mu_\alpha(E',V') < \mu_\alpha(E,V)$ (resp.\ $\le$). Let $G(\alpha;n,d,k)$ denote the moduli space of $\alpha$-stable coherent systems of type $(n,d,k)$. Let $B(n,d,k) \subseteq M(n,d)$ denote the Brill–Noether locus of stable bundles $E$ of rank $n$ and degree $d$ with $h^0(E) \ge k$, and let $U(n,d,k)$ denote the locus of $E \in B(n,d,k)$ with $h^0(E) = k$ (i.e., the coherent systems $(E,V)$ with $V = H^0(E)$).

Fix integers $n \ge 2$ and $k \ge 1$. Does there exist an integer $d_0 = d_0(n,k)$ such that all of the following hold simultaneously?
\begin{enumerate}
\item[(a)] $G(\alpha;n,d,k) \ne \emptyset$ if and only if $\alpha > 0$, $(n-k)\alpha < d$, and $d \ge d_0$;
\item[(b)] $B(n,d,k) \ne \emptyset$ if and only if $d \ge d_0$;
\item[(c)] if $d \ge d_0$, then $U(n,d,k) \ne \emptyset$.
\end{enumerate}

